1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
We're going to take you on the most incredible journey deep in the heart of Africa.
我们将带您踏上一段令人难以置信的旅程，深入非洲的心脏地带。

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:15,000
It's a story of survival against all the odds, with baby orphan elephants making their long and emotional journey back to the wilds, here in Kenya.
这是一段在重重困难中求生的故事。那些失去幼崽的象群，在肯尼亚的野外重新找回属于自己的自由之路，这一路充满了情感与艰辛。

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:21,000
This is where the story starts for all our local orphans.
这就是我们当地所有孤儿故事的开始。

4
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:26,000
When each one of these adorable little babies is rescued, there's just one aim.
当每一个可爱的小婴儿被救起时，只有一个目标。

5
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:34,000
To keep them alive, say that they can eventually go back into the wild, but it's a long heart rate for everyone.
就是让它们活下去，可以说它们最终可以回到野外生活，但这对每个人来说都是漫长的过程。

6
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:44,000
Today on Elephant Power is, I catch up with an old friend who's struggling with an identity crisis.
今天在Elephant Power节目中，我将与一位正在经历身份危机的老朋友重聚。

7
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:50,000
And I'm going to meet a little orphan who I never thought would ever get over her grief after losing her mum.
我还将见到一个孤儿，我原本以为她永远无法走出失去母亲的悲伤。

8
00:00:50,000 --> 00:01:00,000
And a baby elephant is rescued after collapsing from malnutrition. He's in a terrible state and the keepers desperately struggle to save his life.
还有一只因营养不良而倒下的小象被救了。它状况非常糟糕，饲养员们正拼命努力挽救它的生命。

9
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:26,000
We're back for a second series to take you behind the scenes of an extraordinary orphanage devoted to saving the lives of baby elephant.
我们将再次播出第二季，带您了解这个致力于拯救小象生命的特殊孤儿院的幕后故事。

10
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:39,000
Every year the David Sheldon Wildlife Trust rescues dozens of little wild orphans from all over Kenya, who's lost their mum's in tragic circumstances, often because of conflict with man.
每年，David Sheldon Wildlife Trust都会从肯尼亚各地拯救数十只因悲剧事件而失去母亲的野生孤儿小象，这些事件往往源于与人类的冲突。

11
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:51,000
We're going to follow some of our stories and see just what it takes to save these vulnerable and traumatised little babies and eventually get them back to the wilds where they belong.
我们将跟随一些相关故事，看看要如何拯救这些脆弱且受创伤的小象，最终让它们回到属于它们的野外生活环境中。

12
00:01:51,000 --> 00:02:02,000
I'll be following the stories of the older orphans at the two release sites in Sava National Park.
我将会关注萨瓦国家公园内两个放归点中那些年纪较大的孤儿象的故事。

13
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:08,000
The elephants here range through two to nine years old. I know they're still young, so they'd be huge.
这些大象的年龄在两到九岁之间。我知道它们还很年轻，所以体型会非常大。

14
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:15,000
It's stuck on me, he could crush me, and he's so gentle.
他似乎无法被我打败，而他又非常温柔。

15
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:27,000
I'm based up in a Kenyan capital with a tiny, near arrivals. Sadly, every one of the little elephants here arrive physically and emotionally traumatised.
我驻扎在肯尼亚的首都，这里只有少数小象刚刚抵达。遗憾的是，所有小象在抵达时都处于身体和情感上的创伤状态。

16
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:45,000
Here in Nairobi is where the healing process begins. Keepers like Edwin and his team devote their lives to trying to save these babies, but despite their best efforts and all the years of experience, just under half of all the elephants rescued, sadly don't make it.
在内罗毕，治愈的过程才刚刚开始。像埃德温这样的饲养员和团队竭尽全力试图拯救这些小象，但尽管他们付出了最大努力，且拥有多年的经验，可仍有不到一半的小象能够活下来。

17
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:54,000
If the elephants survive those first two years, then the trust moves them from Nairobi to here to Sava National Park and what a place this is.
如果这些大象能熬过最初的两年，它们就会被送到萨瓦国家公园，那里真是个绝佳的地方。

18
00:02:54,000 --> 00:03:04,000
And it's here that they learn the skills which will enable them to go back to the wild, because the whole point of saving these elephants is to give them a second chance.
在这里，它们会学习各种技能，从而能够重返野外生活。拯救这些大象的目的，就是给它们第二次机会。

19
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:18,000
But it's not just about learning the rules of survival. With so many young, intelligent and playful animals together, it's also a huge amount of fun.
但这不仅仅是学习生存技能的问题。有这么多年轻、聪明且爱玩的动物在一起，也充满了乐趣。

20
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:37,000
But ultimately this is all about getting these little elephants to bond with each other. They've all lost their real families, but now they have a new one and they'll be friends for life.
但最终，这一切都是为了让这些小象能够彼此建立友谊。它们都失去了真正的家庭，但现在有了新的家庭，它们将成为一生的朋友。

21
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:46,000
All of the elephants here at the orphanage are under two years old, and just like human babies under two, they're growing and changing all the time.
这里孤儿院里的所有大象都不到两岁，就像两岁以下的人类婴儿一样，它们一直在成长和变化。

22
00:03:46,000 --> 00:04:00,000
When I was here a year ago, there was a little elephant that was all about that size, who absolutely captured my heart. She was a sweet little Ellie, but so obviously still very grief-stricken for the trauma of losing her family.
一年前我来到这里时，有一只大小与它们相仿的小象，它真的打动了我的心。它叫埃莉，是个可爱的小象，但显然因为失去家庭而深受创伤。

23
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:11,000
The little elephant was called Lou and Laney. Lou and Laney was orphaned at just four months old and was deeply traumatized when she came in.
这只小象的名字叫卢和莱尼。卢和莱尼在四个月大时便成为孤儿，进入孤儿院后也受到了严重的心理创伤。

24
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:22,000
It's thought she saw her mom being killed by poachers. Headkeeper Edwin gets a close watch over her, but no one was sure that she would ever get over her loss.
人们认为她看到自己的母亲被偷猎者杀死。管理员埃德温非常照顾她，但没人确定她能否从这种创伤中恢复过来。

25
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:41,000
In the last year, Lou and Laney has changed into a very different elephant. She's grown so much. Oh, gorgeous. Last time I saw her, she was so obviously still grieving for the loss of her family, so it went into all that change.
过去一年里，卢和莱尼发生了巨大的变化。它成长了很多。真是美极了。上次见到它时，它显然仍然在为失去家庭而悲伤，所以才发生了如此大的变化。

26
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:52,000
She changed. She started to play with the others. She started to make close friendships with the keepers, and now she's the most playful of her.
它变了。它开始与其他大象一起玩耍。它开始与管理员们建立亲密的友谊，现在它成了最活泼的小象。

27
00:04:52,000 --> 00:05:05,000
She's always the first one to get into the mud and play the others. She's always had a lovely next year. She's always had a lovely next year.
它总是第一个进入泥里玩耍的。它总是拥有美好的未来。它总是拥有美好的未来。

28
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:20,000
It's incredible, isn't it? Yes. She seems so confident now. She's absolutely the matter. She's the mini matriarch. So basically, she's the one that's taken on the role of mothering the little baby.
真不可思议，对吧？是的。现在它看起来非常自信。它完全成了母象的角色。它就是那个负责照顾小象的人。

29
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:28,000
She's the one who's doing that, and she's doing it very well. I always find it incredible, Edwin, how an elephant is, but she must still be under two years old.
它就是这么做的，而且做得很好。埃德温，我总是觉得不可思议，一只大象能做到这样，但它显然还不到两岁。

30
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:36,000
18 months is mothering a little baby like me. Always seven months. Seven months older.
18个月的时间来照顾像我这样的小象，实在太难了。总是7个月大。比我大7个月。

31
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:49,000
Edwin, how do you feel about her becoming the mini matriarch? Well, I'm very happy about her, because when she came in the first place, I didn't think she'd make it. And now she's a big mini matriarch.
埃德温，你觉得她成为小族长怎么样？我其实很高兴，因为当初她出现时，我根本没想到她能成功成为小族长。现在她已经成了出色的小族长了。

32
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:55,000
Which makes us think that she's done a very great job for having brought her all that way.
这让我们觉得，她为了走到这里来，确实做得很出色。

33
00:05:56,000 --> 00:06:07,000
While Michaela catches up with the latest little matriarch in Nairobi, I'm more than 300km south in Voi, one of the two release sites in Savo National Park.
当米凯拉在内罗毕寻找最新的小族长时，我则在南方300公里外的沃伊地区，那里是萨沃国家公园中的两个放养点之一。

34
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:14,000
Savo's 20,000 square kilometres provide a perfect elephant habitat.
萨沃地区的20,000平方公里土地，是大象理想的栖息地。

35
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:29,000
This is where the orphans eventually returned to the wild, and last time we were here, we saw this in action.
就是在这里，那些孤儿最终重返野外，上次我们在这里时，就看到这一幕了。

36
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:42,000
Emily, the 11-year-old matriarch of the herd, felt she was ready to go back to the wild. It was very hard for her to leave all her friends at the stockades.
埃米莉，那群中11岁的族长，感觉自己已经准备好重返野外了。她很难离开所有的朋友，留在围栏里。

37
00:06:42,000 --> 00:06:47,000
But eventually, the time was right, and she disappeared off into the bush.
但最终，时机到了，她便消失在灌木丛中。

38
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:54,000
With so much wilderness out there, no one was sure they would ever see her again.
这么多的野生区域，没人确定还能再见到她。

39
00:06:54,000 --> 00:07:02,000
This is my first time back in Savo for over a year, and guess who's here to meet me?
这是我一年多来第一次回到萨沃地区，猜猜谁会来见我？

40
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:06,000
What a treat.
真是个惊喜。

41
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:11,000
It's Emily.
她是艾米丽。

42
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:21,000
This is the biggest of the orphans, an orphan that's gone back to the wild, and just the loveliest creature.
这是最庞大的孤儿，一个回到野外的孤儿，也是最可爱的生物。

43
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:29,000
She's a giant, and yet she's only 12 years old, gentle, powerful, wise.
她体型巨大，却只有12岁，温柔、强大且智慧。

44
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:32,000
So why is she back?
那么，她为什么回来呢？

45
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:40,000
Maybe because she's feeling hungry, wants to save us a few tidbits, because any minute now, the other orphans are going to be here.
也许是因为她感到饥饿，想为我们留些食物，因为再过一会儿，其他孤儿就会到来。

46
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:44,000
And you know what? I bet you anything you like, she knows that.
你知道吗？我敢打赌，她知道这一点。

47
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:49,000
That runble was probably a communication between her and the other elephants.
那声吼叫可能是她与其他大象之间的交流方式。

48
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:54,000
And here they come. I wonder how they react when they see who's here.
他们来了。我好奇，当他们看到谁在这里时会有什么反应。

49
00:07:54,000 --> 00:08:00,000
Out goes the trunk.
她的象鼻伸了出来。

50
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:04,000
A little bit of the greeting.
这是她打招呼的方式。

51
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:08,000
It's almost as if they come to pay the respects.
几乎就像他们来表达敬意一样。

52
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:14,000
It's just one. Oh, I love it.
只有一个而已。哦，我太喜欢了。

53
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:25,000
And it's almost like hero worship at times. The way these younger elephants, just they're so chuffed to see Emily.
有时甚至就像对英雄的崇拜。那些年轻的大象们，看到艾米丽时真是兴奋极了。

54
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:29,000
Those sprouty sort of grounds, those rumbles.
那些像幼苗一样的地面，还有那些声音。

55
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:34,000
Talking to each other. How are you? How's it been? Long time no see.
互相交谈着。你怎么样？最近过得如何？好久不见。

56
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:42,000
She looks so healthy.
她看起来非常健康。

57
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:47,000
Look at her. Now that she is.
看看她吧。现在她已经这么健康了。

58
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:56,000
And that of course would always be one of the worries. Can the orphans, when they go back to the wild, find enough food?
当然，这始终是一个令人担忧的问题。那些孤儿们回到野外后，能否找到足够的食物呢？

59
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:58,000
There's the proof.
有证据可以证明这一点。

60
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:07,000
Okay. That's the difference. They're going to the orphans inside the wiring closure.
好吧。这就是区别所在。它们会进入被围起来的孤儿所在的地方。

61
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:14,000
An electric fence to keep them in. Emily, obviously still outside, she's back in the wild, has been for over a year.
一个电围栏用来将它们关在里面。艾米丽显然还在外面，她又回到了野外生活，已经一年多了。

62
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:20,000
Obviously thriving. And why is she back here? Just to say hello, old habits die hard.
显然她生活得很好。她为什么又回到这里呢？只是想打个招呼而已，旧习惯很难改掉。

63
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:23,000
A little bit of extra food maybe she's hoping for.
也许她希望得到一些额外的食物吧。

64
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:29,000
But I have absolutely no worries about Emily. She is doing just fine.
但我对艾米丽完全不用担心，她过得很好。

65
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:38,000
Emily came to the orphanage when she was just four weeks old. And now she's living as a wild elephant.
艾米丽在四周大的时候就来到了孤儿院。现在她就像一头野生大象一样生活着。

66
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:47,000
That's exactly what the trust was set up to do. And it's down to the vision and dedication of its founder, Dame Daphne Sheldon.
这正是该信托机构设立的初衷。而这一切都归功于其创始人达芙妮·谢尔登女士的愿景与努力。

67
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:58,000
She has over 50 years of experience in raising orphan baby elephants. And established the trust to try and save as many of Kenya's wild elephants as possible.
她在抚养孤儿象方面拥有超过50年的经验。她设立该信托机构，旨在拯救肯尼亚尽可能多的野生大象。

68
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:08,000
She has a team of 49 high skilled keepers who spend 24 hours a day looking after these surprisingly fragile little creatures.
她有一支由49名技术精湛的饲养员组成的团队，他们每天24小时照顾这些脆弱的小动物。

69
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:14,000
They help to give back to the babies the will to live when they're grieving for their lost families.
当这些小象因失去家人而悲伤时，他们帮助它们重新获得生存的意愿。

70
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:23,000
But the real key to piecing back together the lives of these little elephants is having the companionship of other orphans.
但让这些小象重新过上正常生活的关键，就是有其他孤儿们的陪伴。

71
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:31,000
Look at this. This is a really special little bomb that's developed in recent weeks.
看看这个吧。这是最近几周研发出的一个非常特别的小“炸弹”装置。

72
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:39,000
This is Lou Elaney and this is McKenna. And they are never apart. Wherever Lou Elaney goes, McKenna is right by her side.
这是Lou Elaney，还有McKenna。她们从来不会分开，无论Lou Elaney走到哪里，McKenna都会紧随其后。

73
00:10:39,000 --> 00:10:46,000
And usually doing this. You see what she's doing? She's sucking. Lou Elaney's ear. You see there's a wet patch here.
通常都是这样。你看到她在做什么吗？她正在吮吸Lou Elaney的耳朵。你看，这里有个湿痕。

74
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:53,000
This is where she's been permanently sucking. Now I have to say I think I find that slightly irritated her for a while.
这就是她一直吮吸的地方。我想，这确实让她暂时有些不适。

75
00:10:54,000 --> 00:11:02,000
This is such a special little elephant. So patient and so loving. You're a gorgeous elephant you.
这真是一头特别可爱的小象啊。如此耐心又充满爱意。你真是一头美丽的象啊。

76
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:08,000
The you. You're such an easy old friend.
你啊，真是个好朋友。

77
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:18,000
Both Lou Elaney and McKenna saw their mothers killed by poachers. So it's wonderful that they're able to give such comfort to each other.
Lou Elaney和McKenna都目睹过自己的母亲被偷猎者杀害的惨剧。因此，她们能够互相给予安慰，真是很棒。

78
00:11:19,000 --> 00:11:22,000
The team here is always ready to take in any babies who need help.
这里的团队随时准备帮助任何需要帮助的小动物。

79
00:11:22,000 --> 00:11:32,000
Daphne's daughter Angela has just taken a call about a tiny elephant in distress. And a full-scale rescue has been launched.
Daphne的女儿Angela刚刚接到电话，说有一头小象处于困境中。于是，一个全面的救援行动就此展开。

80
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:45,000
A team of keepers from the trust socket in boy have been sent to see if they can help the little calf.
来自该机构的护理团队被派去帮助那头小牛。

81
00:11:46,000 --> 00:11:50,000
It's too weak to stand falling in and out of consciousness.
它太虚弱了，无法维持意识。

82
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:55,000
Its mother is desperately trying to revive it, but the calf looks close to death.
它的母亲正拼命试图让它恢复意识，但这只小牛看起来几乎已经死亡。

83
00:11:55,000 --> 00:12:07,000
The team will only intervene if there is no other hope for the baby. So they're waiting to see what the mother is going to do.
只有当没有其他办法挽救这只小牛时，团队才会出手干预。因此他们正在等待母亲的下一步行动。

84
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:20,000
The keepers sees their chance. Now it's a race against time to get him to the vet at the nearby stockade.
饲养员们看到了机会。现在必须争分夺秒地将它送到附近的兽医诊所。

85
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:41,000
The poor little calf is severely malnourished and dehydrated. The only hope is to try and get him to drink something.
这只可怜的小牛严重营养不良且脱水。唯一的希望就是让它喝点东西。

86
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:47,000
There are some rehydration fluids and although desperately weak, he manages to suck.
有一些补水液，虽然它非常虚弱，但还是能够吸吮。

87
00:12:47,000 --> 00:12:57,000
The stockades here in boy are set up to look after much older elephants.
这里的饲养所是用来照顾年纪较大的大象的。

88
00:12:57,000 --> 00:13:05,000
This little bull urgently needs to go up to the orphanage in Nairobi where he can get intensive care in purpose-filled stables.
这只小公象急需被送到内罗毕的孤儿院，在那里它可以在专门的马厩中接受精心照料。

89
00:13:06,000 --> 00:13:13,000
But it's too late to fly him out today so the little elephant is moved into one of the keepers runs for the night.
但今天已经来不及把它空运出去了，所以这只小象被安置在饲养员们的营地里过夜。

90
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:21,000
If he makes it to the morning then he'll be flown up to Daphne in her team, but at the moment things are not looking promising.
如果它能活到早上，就会被空运到达芙妮所在的团队那里，但目前情况并不乐观。

91
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:39,000
At the Nairobi orphanage the baby is ahead into their beds and it's little McKenna leading this mini stampede.
在内罗毕孤儿院里，小 McKenna走在其他幼象的前面，带领着这群小象一起奔跑。

92
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:47,000
Each Ellie has their own individual stables. A keeper sleeps in there with them giving them comfort and milk throughout the night.
每只Ellie都有自己专用的马厩。饲养员会在那里与它们同睡，整夜为它们提供安慰和牛奶。

93
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:59,000
At seven months old McKenna is one of the youngest elephants at the orphanage.
七个月大的 McKenna是孤儿院里最年幼的大象之一。

94
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:05,000
She lost her real mum when she was just seven weeks old and was found wandering alone in the bush.
她七周大的时候就失去了真正的母亲，后来被发现独自在丛林中流浪。

95
00:14:05,000 --> 00:14:11,000
So she takes great comfort from knowing that her adoptive mum, Luilania, is right next door.
因此，知道她的养母Luilania就在隔壁，让她感到非常安心。

96
00:14:11,000 --> 00:14:17,000
Luilania doors McKenna too and there reparts to this job.
McKenna也去拜访Luilania，然后继续她的工作。

97
00:14:17,000 --> 00:14:21,000
She gets to help herself to some of her little friends suck her.
她可以帮自己的小伙伴们吸奶。

98
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:38,000
But McKenna doesn't mind, she's completely exhausted after a long and exciting day out in the bush.
不过 McKenna并不介意，因为她在丛林里度过漫长而刺激的一天后，已经筋疲力尽。

99
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:47,000
And devoted head keeper Edwin is ready with her blanket.
忠诚的饲养员Edwin则随时准备为她提供毯子。

100
00:14:47,000 --> 00:14:53,000
Six years ago he gave up a career as a priest to look after these amazing little animals.
六年前，他放弃了神职人员的职业，来照顾这些神奇的小动物。

101
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:05,000
This is a good baby. She's come to see it so quickly.
这是个好宝宝，她来得如此之快。

102
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:10,000
What's it like to share a stable with an elephant?
与大象一起住在马厩里是什么感觉？

103
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:20,000
Where the meat might look strange, it might look funny, but having gotten used to find it normal, find it fine.
虽然肉看起来可能很奇怪，但一旦习惯了，就会觉得这很正常。

104
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:26,000
What did you think when they first asked them there? When they first said you got to stay without elephant all night in the stable?
当他们第一次问你这个问题时，你怎么想？当他们说你整晚不得不在马厩里不跟大象在一起时，你是什么反应？

105
00:15:27,000 --> 00:15:32,000
I was shy. I didn't know what was going to happen in the night.
我很害羞，不知道晚上会发生什么。

106
00:15:32,000 --> 00:15:40,000
And so it was a bit worried and a game slip, keeping an eye, waiting to see what will happen.
所以，我有点担心，也有点紧张，一直盯着情况，等待看会发生什么。

107
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:44,000
But after a lot of weeks I got used to and it's normal.
但经过几周后，我就习惯了，现在一切都正常了。

108
00:15:44,000 --> 00:15:47,000
Like a normal routine with a baby at home.
就像家里有宝宝后的正常生活一样。

109
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:50,000
Did that only last about 18 months?
那段时间只持续了18个月吗？

110
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:52,000
Do you have six or seven years?
你有六七年了吗？

111
00:15:52,000 --> 00:15:54,000
Yes, yes.
是的，没错。

112
00:15:54,000 --> 00:15:55,000
Do you get tired?
你感到疲惫吗？

113
00:15:56,000 --> 00:15:57,000
One point you do.
你确实有一个优点。

114
00:15:57,000 --> 00:15:58,000
Yes.
是的。

115
00:15:58,000 --> 00:16:03,000
And why do you give so much to these orphans?
那你为什么要如此帮助这些孤儿呢？

116
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:05,000
It's because they need it.
因为他们需要帮助。

117
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:12,000
If you don't devote to them, then there will be stress a lot and they might die.
如果你不帮助他们，就会面临很大的压力，他们可能会死去。

118
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:20,000
So you have to commit yourself to them and in order for them to survive.
所以你必须致力于帮助他们，才能让他们活下去。

119
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:26,000
It just won't be harder.
这样就不会那么艰难了。

120
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:40,000
Don't they dream about us?
他们不希望我们吗？

121
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:58,000
Early morning in Sarpo and the older orphans are up and about.
清晨时分，萨波的那些年长孤儿们已经起床活动了。

122
00:16:58,000 --> 00:17:02,000
But as the tiny rescued calf made it through the night.
不过，那只被救下的小牛儿却熬过了那个夜晚。

123
00:17:02,000 --> 00:17:14,000
To everyone's surprise, he's alive and he's up on his feet.
令所有人惊讶的是，它还活着，能够站立起来。

124
00:17:14,000 --> 00:17:19,000
A plane has arrived to take him to Nairobi where he can get specialized treatment.
有一架飞机来接它去内罗毕，那里有专门的治疗措施。

125
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:30,000
After an hour's flight it's only a short flight.
一小时的飞行其实并不长。

126
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:37,000
After an hour's flight it's only a short flight.
一小时的飞行其实并不长。

127
00:17:37,000 --> 00:17:52,000
As soon as the little calf arrives, everyone rushes to help carry him to the stable.
小牛儿一到，大家都赶紧帮忙把它抬到马厩里。

128
00:17:53,000 --> 00:17:56,000
He's so weak he can barely stand on his own.
它太虚弱了，几乎无法独自站立。

129
00:17:56,000 --> 00:17:58,000
Let alone he walk.
更不用说走路了。

130
00:17:58,000 --> 00:18:05,000
Daphne is on hand to meet the little chap as soon as he arrives.
达芙妮会在小牛儿到达时立刻来迎接它。

131
00:18:05,000 --> 00:18:16,000
She's a world expert on rearing baby elephants and immediately goes to work with some homeopathic medicine.
她是饲养小象方面的专家，立刻开始使用顺势疗法药物来照料它。

132
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:27,000
Daphne estimates the little calf to be about three weeks old.
达芙妮估计那头小牛大约三周大。

133
00:18:27,000 --> 00:18:31,000
He's been named under Lolo after the area where he was found.
根据它被发现的地点，它被命名为“洛洛”。

134
00:18:31,000 --> 00:18:34,000
I'm very dehydrated.
我严重脱水了。

135
00:18:34,000 --> 00:18:38,000
It's not quite a skin here.
这里并不算完整的皮肤。

136
00:18:38,000 --> 00:18:48,000
The problem with these sort of babies is you know when you start rehydrating them often the kidneys collapse.
这类幼崽的问题在于，当开始给它们补水时，肾脏往往会受损。

137
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:51,000
So that's a problem, you know.
所以这就是一个问题。

138
00:18:53,000 --> 00:19:04,000
But we can just try you know lots of rehydration just a little bit of milk to begin with because you know that can really mess up his stomach and he can't force it to have a bout of diarrhea.
不过我们可以尝试大量补水，至少先给它一些牛奶，因为那样会严重损害它的肠胃，它无法强制自己腹泻。

139
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:13,000
He's in pretty poor shape and I think probably one of the worst that we've had coming.
它的状况非常糟糕，我想这是我们遇到过最糟糕的情况之一。

140
00:19:13,000 --> 00:19:18,000
He's very very dehydrated, emaciated obviously a starvation victim.
它严重脱水，明显是饥饿导致的消瘦。

141
00:19:19,000 --> 00:19:29,000
He hasn't had his mother's milk back a long time and he's got something seriously wrong with one eye and the other one doesn't look too good either.
他已经很久没有喝到母亲的奶了，他的一只眼睛有问题，另一只眼睛也状况不佳。

142
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:33,000
So he's got problems with his eyes definitely.
显然，他的眼睛存在问题。

143
00:19:33,000 --> 00:19:39,000
Under Lolo will need round the clock pair if he's to stand any chance of survival.
如果想要有生存机会，他在洛洛下方必须随时配备一双眼睛。

144
00:19:42,000 --> 00:19:48,000
If the little calf makes it then in two years time he'll be coming back here to save him.
如果小牛能活下来，两年后它就会回来救他。

145
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:53,000
I'm on my way to a thumber the second of the two release sites.
我正在前往两个放生地点的其中一处的路上。

146
00:19:53,000 --> 00:19:59,000
Now it's over a year since I last saw the elephants so I can't wait to see how they're doing.
自从上次见到大象已经过去一年了，我迫不及待想看看它们现在的情况如何。

147
00:20:01,000 --> 00:20:10,000
A thumber is around three hours drive north from the voice blockade where under Lolo was rescued and it's a more remote and wild part of Sarvo.
从洛洛被救的地方向北行驶大约三小时就能到达一个名为“thumber”的地方，那里是萨尔沃地区较为偏僻、野生的地方。

148
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:16,000
There's plenty of food up here and less humans, elephant paradise.
这里食物丰富，人类较少，简直就是大象的天堂。

149
00:20:16,000 --> 00:20:22,000
It's always an early start for L.A.L. is here at a phone, but in fact it's a bit of a fun fact.
L.A.L.总是很早出发，其实这其实是个有趣的事实。

150
00:20:22,000 --> 00:20:28,000
They can't wait to get out of it to all that bush to be wild out of it and that's a whole point right now.
他们迫不及待地想离开这里，去那些茂密的丛林中自由生活，这正是目前他们想要的事情。

151
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:35,000
The 19 orphans that make up the thumber herd sleep in a stockade each night.
那群由19头孤儿组成的象群，每晚都住在围栏里休息。

152
00:20:35,000 --> 00:20:41,000
The daytime is all about learning the skills they need to survive on their own in the wild.
白天，它们则学习在野外独立生存所需的技能。

153
00:20:41,000 --> 00:20:48,000
It's a well-established and happy family and everyone seems to know their place.
这是一个稳定而和谐的家庭，每个人都很清楚自己的位置。

154
00:20:48,000 --> 00:20:55,000
But there's one elephant who the keepers feel is having a struggle with her position in the herd and that's Wendy.
但有一头大象，饲养员觉得它难以适应群体中的角色，那就是温迪。

155
00:20:58,000 --> 00:21:05,000
I've known her for a couple of years now and she was always a very confident outgoing elephant.
我认识她已经几年了，她一直都是一只非常自信且外向的象。

156
00:21:05,000 --> 00:21:14,000
Despite being rescued when she was just days old she thrived in the Nairobi nursery, eventually becoming the mini matriarch up there.
尽管她在几天大时就被救了，但她在内罗毕的育婴院里茁壮成长，最终成为了那里的小族长。

157
00:21:14,000 --> 00:21:24,000
When she was two years old she was moved here to a thumber to join some older orphans and start her reintroduction back to the wild.
当她两岁时，被转移到另一个象群中，与一些年长的孤儿一起，开始重新回归野外生活。

158
00:21:25,000 --> 00:21:30,000
It all started very well but in recent months something has changed.
一切开始时都很顺利，但最近几个月情况发生了变化。

159
00:21:30,000 --> 00:21:43,000
Then the head keeper says despite being one of the most playful characters in the herd when this become a bit of a loner preferring the company of humans.
然后，饲养员说，虽然温迪是群中最活泼的象之一，但现在它却变得比较独来独往，更喜欢与人类在一起。

160
00:21:43,000 --> 00:21:54,000
You know when Wendy first came here when we first brought her from Nairobi we were thinking that really we take the pressure off her because we were bringing bigger elephants to this area.
当温迪第一次被从内罗毕带到这里时，我们以为这样就能减轻她的压力，因为我们会把更大的象带到这个区域。

161
00:21:54,000 --> 00:22:00,000
So they would be the matriarch and that would sort of just allow Wendy to be what she is a young elephant.
因此，她会成为族长，这样温迪就能保持自己年轻大象的本性。

162
00:22:00,000 --> 00:22:07,000
She could just relax no pressure and we thought that would help her but it hasn't quite worked out like that.
她可以放松下来，不必有压力，我们认为这会对她有帮助，但实际情况并非如此。

163
00:22:07,000 --> 00:22:18,000
Instead of helping Wendy it appears almost as if it sort of put her nose out of join and to me that's a reflection on what intelligent animals these are because she doesn't really have a role anymore.
似乎这并没有帮助温迪，反而让她与群体脱节了。在我看来，这反映出这些动物并不聪明，因为她已经没有角色可扮演了。

164
00:22:19,000 --> 00:22:29,000
Instead of being a matriarch she's suddenly sort of nothing within the group and what that seems to have done is to make her turn back towards people, her human family.
她不再扮演族长的角色，在群体中几乎变得无足轻重，这似乎让她重新转向人类家族。

165
00:22:29,000 --> 00:22:37,000
Maybe because Wendy was rescued as a newborn and never really new life with her wild man.
也许是因为温迪在新生时就被救了，她从未真正与野生的丈夫生活在一起。

166
00:22:37,000 --> 00:22:42,000
She's particularly people focused but in the wild female elephants live in hers.
她特别依赖人类，但在野外，雌性大象则独自生活。

167
00:22:42,000 --> 00:22:45,000
Being a loner is not normally an option.
独居通常不是她的选择。

168
00:22:48,000 --> 00:22:55,000
Well one thing about Wendy even if she's a little bit lonely right now she was always a tremendous character.
虽然温迪现在有点孤独，但她一直都是个很出色的角色。

169
00:22:55,000 --> 00:23:02,000
She's got a will of her own I think at some point further down the road she will be a matriarch again.
她有自己的意志，我认为过一段时间后，她会再次成为族长。

170
00:23:02,000 --> 00:23:17,000
Wendy is just four years old so it's not surprising that she's still a bit naughty but this is exactly the time she should be turning away from the humans in her life back towards her elephant family.
温迪才四岁，所以她还有点调皮并不奇怪，但现在正是她应该从人类身边回到大象家族身边的时候。

171
00:23:17,000 --> 00:23:21,000
Well I reckon it's probably time to get her back to the rest of the herd.
我觉得现在可能是时候把她带回其他大象群中了。

172
00:23:21,000 --> 00:23:27,000
Shall we see if we can encourage her back to join the others?
我们试试能否鼓励她重新加入其他大象呢？

173
00:23:27,000 --> 00:23:39,000
That just shows her incredibly important.
这足以说明她的重要性了。

174
00:23:39,000 --> 00:23:47,000
The keepers are still in the lives of these elephants particularly with Wendy here and she sort of wants to be apart from the rest of the herd but she has to keep in contact with them.
这些大象的饲养人员仍然与它们生活在一起，尤其是温迪在身边时，她似乎想远离其他大象，但同时又必须与它们保持联系。

175
00:23:47,000 --> 00:23:51,000
It's not safer. I have to just go wandering off in the bush and it just amazes me.
那样并不安全。我只能在丛林中漫步，真是令人惊讶。

176
00:23:51,000 --> 00:23:57,000
I had just a few little words, a little bit of encouragement and a great big extraordinary creature like that.
我只说了几句话，给予了一些鼓励，而她却是一个如此非凡的生物。

177
00:23:57,000 --> 00:23:59,000
That's what it's told.
就是这么说的。

178
00:24:02,000 --> 00:24:11,000
I'm joining up with the rest of the herd to head out into the bush. I want to see for myself just how bad when this problem is.
我会和其余大象一起前往丛林里。我想亲自看看这个问题到底有多严重。

179
00:24:18,000 --> 00:24:26,000
Every day the elephants here in Athumba spend up to 12 hours learning the ropes and getting used to living out in the wild.
阿通巴的大象们每天要花费多达12小时来学习如何适应野外生活。

180
00:24:26,000 --> 00:24:31,000
They'll walk up to 10km each day with the keepers at their side.
它们每天可以行走10公里，而且有饲养人员陪伴着它们。

181
00:24:31,000 --> 00:24:36,000
The highlight of the day is their visit to the water hall.
这一天的亮点就是他们参观水馆的情景。

182
00:24:36,000 --> 00:24:46,000
Savo has a reputation for being a tough aridary and at times the water halls can dry up completely but not today.
萨沃以干旱恶劣著称，有时水馆里的水会完全干涸，但今天并非如此。

183
00:24:47,000 --> 00:24:54,000
The rains have transformed if you've got a lot of flies you've got dragonflies and of course other elephants are having a ball.
雨水使得环境发生了变化：如果有很多苍蝇，就会出现蜻蜓；当然，其他大象也过得非常愉快。

184
00:24:54,000 --> 00:24:56,000
They're so much closer.
它们离得近多了。

185
00:24:56,000 --> 00:24:58,000
Of course all the water as well.
当然，所有的水也都在那里。

186
00:24:58,000 --> 00:25:02,000
Just like kids at the beach really isn't it?
就像海滩上的孩子一样，对吧？

187
00:25:02,000 --> 00:25:05,000
You can tell these elephants are having an absolute ball.
你可以看出这些大象正玩得非常开心。

188
00:25:17,000 --> 00:25:25,000
[Music]
[音乐]

189
00:25:25,000 --> 00:25:29,000
So where's Wendy while all this is going on?
那么，在这一切发生的时候，温迪在哪里呢？

190
00:25:29,000 --> 00:25:35,000
She's doing exactly what the keepers have said, standing all by herself on the sidelines.
她正按照管理员说的那样做，独自站在一边。

191
00:25:35,000 --> 00:25:38,000
She looks as if she's in a world of her own.
她看起来仿佛处于一个属于自己的世界里。

192
00:25:40,000 --> 00:25:50,000
Wendy's obviously struggling with something but definitely in the keepers looking after the emotional as well as the physical well being of all the elephants.
温迪显然在应对着某些问题，但显然有工作人员在负责照顾这些大象的身心状况。

193
00:25:50,000 --> 00:25:57,000
So they're working hard to find a solution but with an elephant as intelligent as Wendy this won't be easy.
他们正在努力寻找解决方案，但像温迪这样聪明的大象，事情肯定不会那么容易。

194
00:26:02,000 --> 00:26:09,000
Up in Nairobi everybody always joins in the fun as this is a particularly happy bonded her.
在内罗毕，每个人总是积极参与其中，因为这里是一个非常欢乐的地方。

195
00:26:10,000 --> 00:26:29,000
[Music]
[音乐]

196
00:26:29,000 --> 00:26:36,000
They're really enjoying all that love and water. They can see especially the bigger ones that are really getting stuck in.
它们非常享受这种爱与水的环境。尤其是那些体型较大的大象，它们被卡住了。

197
00:26:36,000 --> 00:26:42,000
Now we talk about these larger elephants as being the nature of what they do.
现在我们来谈谈那些体型较大的大象，它们的行为本质上就是如此。

198
00:26:42,000 --> 00:26:47,000
And we forget that actually babies themselves, now these elephants are older than two years.
我们却忘记了，这些大象现在已经超过两岁了，它们也有自己的孩子。

199
00:26:47,000 --> 00:26:53,000
And although they take on that nurturing role and that caring role, sometimes they just want to have fun.
虽然它们承担着养育和照顾的责任，但有时它们也只想享受快乐时光。

200
